{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/bench/yin_vm_bench.cljc src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd_v2.cljd; rg -n 'session|defn run-on-stream|throw|observe-next' src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc; rg -n 'restore-initial-env|defn.*eval|reset' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc; cat deps.edn\"","aggregated_output":"(ns bench.yin-vm-bench\n  \"Semantic VM Phase 4: the ast-walker against the linear semantic VM on\n   `yin.vm` (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md` §8).\n\n   The workload is the historic tail-recursive countdown from the deleted\n   `yin.vm.bytecode-bench`, so the ratios read against the 1.32x walker and\n   1.0–1.1x register/stack line in `docs/cesk-space-optimization.md`.\n\n   The timed region is `vm/run` alone. VM construction, AST → datoms, the\n   lowering, and the program load stay outside it. Each timed call runs the\n   same loaded VM value: both machines are persistent values and the\n   countdown touches no stream, so no reset is needed between runs.\n\n   JVM (Criterium quick-bench):\n     clj -Sdeps '{:aliases {:bench {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]}}}' \\\\\n       -M:bench -m bench.yin-vm-bench 500 5000\n   Node:\n     clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile vm-bench\n     node target/vm-bench.js 500 5000\"\n  (:require #?(:cljd [] :clj [criterium.core :as criterium])\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic])\n  #?(:cljd (:import [\"dart:core\" DateTime])))\n\n\n(defn tail-countdown-ast\n  [n]\n  (let [self-fn {:type :lambda,\n                 :params ['self 'n],\n                 :body {:type :if,\n                        :test {:type :application,\n                               :operator {:type :variable, :name '<},\n                               :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'n}\n                                          {:type :literal, :value 1}]},\n                        :consequent {:type :literal, :value 0},\n                        :alternate\n                        {:type :application,\n                         :operator {:type :variable, :name 'self},\n                         :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'self}\n                                    {:type :application,\n                                     :operator {:type :variable, :name '-},\n                                     :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'n}\n                                                {:type :literal, :value 1}]}],\n                         :tail? true},\n                        :tail? true}}]\n    {:type :application,\n     :operator self-fn,\n     :operands [self-fn {:type :literal, :value n}],\n     :tail? true}))\n\n\n(defn load-walker\n  [ast]\n  (ast-walker/vm-load-program (ast-walker/create-vm) (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n\n\n(defn load-semantic\n  [ast]\n  (semantic/vm-load-program (semantic/create-vm) (linearize/lower-ast ast)))\n\n\n(def evaluators\n  [[\"AST Walker\" load-walker] [\"Semantic\" load-semantic]])\n\n\n(defn- check!\n  [label loaded]\n  (let [v (vm/value (vm/run loaded))]\n    (when-not (= 0 v)\n      (throw (ex-info \"Benchmark workload returned the wrong value\"\n                      {:evaluator label, :value v})))))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj\n   (defn- measure-ms\n     \"Criterium quick-bench mean, in milliseconds.\"\n     [loaded]\n     (let [result (criterium/quick-benchmark (vm/run loaded) {})]\n       (criterium/report-result result)\n       (* 1e3 (first (:mean result))))))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj nil\n   :cljs\n   (defn- measure-ms\n     \"Mean of 9 samples after 4 warmups, each sample 20 runs, in milliseconds\n      per run — the sampling discipline of `yin.register-bench-cljd-v2`.\"\n     [loaded]\n     (let [now #(.now js/performance)\n           sample (fn []\n                    (let [start (now)]\n                      (dotimes [_ 20] (vm/run loaded))\n                      (/ (- (now) start) 20)))]\n       (dotimes [_ 4] (sample))\n       (let [samples (vec (repeatedly 9 sample))]\n         (println \"  samples ms/run:\" samples)\n         (/ (reduce + samples) (count samples))))))\n\n\n(defn run-bench\n  [ns-list]\n  (doseq [n ns-list]\n    (let [ast (tail-countdown-ast n)\n          means (into {}\n                      (for [[label load] evaluators]\n                        (let [loaded (load ast)]\n                          (check! label loaded)\n                          (println (str \"\\n\" label \" n=\" n))\n                          [label (measure-ms loaded)])))\n          walker (get means \"AST Walker\")]\n      (println (str \"\\nRESULT n=\" n))\n      (doseq [[label _] evaluators]\n        (let [ms (get means label)]\n          (println (str \"  \" label \": \" ms \" ms/run, \"\n                        (/ ms walker) \"x walker\")))))))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj\n   (defn -main\n     [& args]\n     (run-bench (if (seq args) (map #(Long/parseLong %) args) [500 5000]))\n     (shutdown-agents)))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj nil\n   :cljs\n   (defn -main\n     [& args]\n     (run-bench (if (seq args) (map #(js/parseInt %) args) [500 5000]))))\n(ns yin.register-bench-cljd-v2\n  \"Benchmark the Yin VM v2 evaluators on Dart.\n\n   `yin.register-bench-cljd` drove the v1 register VM. This benchmark drives\n   `yin.vm.ast-walker` and the linear `yin.vm.semantic` VM\n   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md` §8) on one workload, and its numbers\n   are not comparable with the v1 register numbers. The workload and the\n   sampling discipline are carried over unchanged so the runs answer the\n   same question about their own engine.\n\n   The timed region is `vm/run` alone. VM construction, the lowering, and the\n   program load stay outside it: the program is loaded once, and each\n   iteration resets to that loaded program and runs it, which is the v2\n   idiom for re-running one program (v2's `reset` preserves `:program`).\n\n   Compile and run:\n     clj -M:cljd compile yin.register-bench-cljd-v2\n     dart run bin/register_bench_cljd_v2.dart\"\n  (:require [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic])\n  (:import [\"dart:core\" DateTime]))\n\n\n(def ^:private benchmark-config\n  {:workload :tail-countdown,\n   :iterations 20,\n   :samples 9,\n   :warmup 4,\n   :countdown-n 50000})\n\n\n(def ^:private stream-capacity 1024)\n\n\n(defn- now-ms\n  []\n  (/ (.-microsecondsSinceEpoch (DateTime/now)) 1000.0))\n\n\n(defn- mean\n  [xs]\n  (/ (reduce + 0 xs) (count xs)))\n\n\n(defn- median\n  [xs]\n  (let [sorted (vec (sort xs))\n        n (count sorted)\n        mid (quot n 2)]\n    (if (odd? n)\n      (nth sorted mid)\n      (/ (+ (nth sorted (dec mid)) (nth sorted mid)) 2.0))))\n\n\n(defn- closure-call-ast\n  []\n  {:type :application,\n   :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['x], :body {:type :variable, :name 'x}},\n   :operands [{:type :literal, :value 42}]})\n\n\n(defn- tail-countdown-ast\n  [n]\n  (let [self-fn {:type :lambda,\n                 :params ['self 'n],\n                 :body {:type :if,\n                        :test {:type :application,\n                               :operator {:type :variable, :name '<},\n                               :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'n}\n                                          {:type :literal, :value 1}]},\n                        :consequent {:type :literal, :value 0},\n                        :alternate\n                        {:type :application,\n                         :operator {:type :variable, :name 'self},\n                         :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'self}\n                                    {:type :application,\n                                     :operator {:type :variable, :name '-},\n                                     :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'n}\n                                                {:type :literal, :value 1}]}],\n                         :tail? true},\n                        :tail? true}}]\n    {:type :application,\n     :operator self-fn,\n     :operands [self-fn {:type :literal, :value n}],\n     :tail? true}))\n\n\n(defn- workload->ast\n  [{:keys [workload countdown-n]}]\n  (case workload\n    :closure-call (closure-call-ast)\n    :tail-countdown (tail-countdown-ast countdown-n)\n    (throw (ex-info \"Unknown benchmark workload\" {:workload workload}))))\n\n\n(defn- make-stream\n  \"The `:make-stream` the composition hands the VM. A nil capacity is the\n   VM's default, not an unbounded stream.\"\n  [capacity]\n  (ringbuffer/create!\n    {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\n     ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\n\n\n(defn- load-program\n  \"Construct the VM and load the workload. Construction is all-or-nothing in\n   v2, so a non-`ok` stream outcome throws here rather than half-building.\n   The semantic VM refuses an AST in `eval`, so its program is lowered and\n   loaded explicitly, and it is then run once like the walker's.\"\n  [evaluator ast]\n  (let [opts {:primitives vm/primitives, :make-stream make-stream}]\n    (case evaluator\n      :ast-walker (vm/eval (ast-walker/create-vm opts) ast)\n      :semantic (vm/run (semantic/vm-load-program\n                          (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                          (linearize/lower-ast ast))))))\n\n\n(defn- run-iterations\n  \"Run the already-loaded program `iterations` times. `reset` restores\n   `:control` from the loaded `:program` and clears the CESK state; `run`\n   executes it.\"\n  [program iterations]\n  (dotimes [_ iterations] (vm/run (vm/reset program))))\n\n\n(defn- sample-total-ms\n  [program iterations]\n  (let [start (now-ms)]\n    (run-iterations program iterations)\n    (- (now-ms) start)))\n\n\n(defn main\n  []\n  (doseq [evaluator [:ast-walker :semantic]]\n    (let [{:keys [workload iterations samples warmup], :as cfg} benchmark-config\n          ast (workload->ast cfg)\n          program (load-program evaluator ast)]\n      (dotimes [_ warmup] (run-iterations program iterations))\n      (let [sample-total (vec (for [_ (range samples)]\n                                (sample-total-ms program iterations)))\n            sample-per-iter (mapv #(/ % iterations) sample-total)]\n        (println (str \"workload=\" workload\n                      \" evaluator=\" (name evaluator) \"-v2\"\n                      \" iterations=\" iterations\n                      \" samples=\" samples\n                      \" warmup=\" warmup))\n        (when (= workload :tail-countdown)\n          (println (str \"countdown_n=\" (:countdown-n cfg))))\n        (println (str \"stream_capacity=\" stream-capacity))\n        (println (str \"sample_total_ms=\" sample-total))\n        (println (str \"sample_per_iter_ms=\" sample-per-iter))\n        (println (str \"RESULT mean_total_ms=\" (mean sample-total)\n                      \" median_total_ms=\" (median sample-total)\n                      \" mean_per_iter_ms=\" (mean sample-per-iter)\n                      \" median_per_iter_ms=\" (median sample-per-iter)))))))\n10:   how a session resumes from where it stopped. The observer never creates,\n31:   Exports exactly `attach`, `observe-next`, and `run-on-stream`.\"\n43:   without the reader surface throw exactly as `attach` documents.\"\n48:      (throw (ex-info \"Stream attachment failed\"\n54:          (throw (ex-info \"Attached handle declares no reader surface\"\n62:   throw.\n68:   without minting one: the composition resuming a session knows where its\n75:   non-`ok` attachment or cursor outcome throws `ex-info` preserving the\n86:       (throw (ex-info \"Observer cursor could not be minted\"\n106:  (throw (ex-info message\n132:  \"This observer's policy for a step defect: throw, naming the outcome the\n153:(defn observe-next\n162:   unexpected ones throw with the original outcome preserved.\"\n184:  \"The consumer state a failing `run` left, for the carried session.\n186:   A `run` that made partial progress before throwing — a flush that\n199:(defn- carry-session\n200:  \"Rethrow `e`, keeping the throw and carrying the partial session in the\n203:   The original message and data are preserved and `:session` is added. The\n204:   rethrow is a new `ExceptionInfo` whose cause is the original, so a caller\n207:   does not read `:session` keeps the old semantics — a throw means the\n209:   session, which names the furthest progress the round had made where the\n211:  [session e]\n212:  (throw (ex-info (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n213:                  (assoc (ex-data e) :session session)\n217:(defn run-on-stream\n218:  \"Coordinate one `{:observer observer :consumer consumer}` session over the\n219:   attached medium, returning the updated session.\n230:   recovery cursor and continues; `blocked` and `end` return the session.\n232:   next batch, and one that is not returns the session without another read.\n234:   A `load` or `run` that throws still propagates — the throw is kept — but\n235:   carries the partial session in the exception's data under `:session`, so\n237:   session: a throwing `load` carries the cursor *before* the failing batch,\n238:   so a retry re-reads it; a throwing `run` carries the cursor *after* the\n241:   progress before throwing, else the state `load` returned — so a retry\n243:   terminal read after processed batches carries the session those batches\n245:   as data from `load` rather than throw, and reserve the throw for its own\n247:  [session ready? load run]\n248:  (loop [{:keys [observer consumer]} session]\n252:                             (carry-session\n260:      ;; returned: a throwing load propagates before any successor exists, and\n261:      ;; the session it carries names the cursor before the failing batch.\n269:                            (carry-session {:observer observer, :consumer consumer} e)))]\n273:                         ;; a throwing run carries the post-batch cursor and the\n279:                                          (carry-session\n292:                 (carry-session {:observer observer, :consumer consumer} e))))))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:645:(defn- vm-reset\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:657:(defn- vm-eval\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:668:    (engine/restore-initial-env initial-env res)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:679:  (reset [vm] (vm-reset vm))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:92:(defn restore-initial-env\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-